# Fictional EP Tracklist

## 1. Bay Four Walks Ahead of the Crates

**Story & Context:** The debut runs at 104 BPM. Rūta opens with an eight-note kanklės ostinato alternating low tonic, upper fifth, suspended second, and a damped bass return. Ellis enters after four bars with snare drags that repeatedly begin just before her upper-string accents while the bass drum lands slightly early on selected downbeats. Milda adds one clipped prepared-piano fourth every two bars. Jonas waits until the second cycle to introduce a two-note baritone-horn call that lands late against the grid. Sofija answers with a low bass-clarinet ascent that resolves before the next kanklės loop.

At the midpoint, the band executes its first full Corner Turn: Ellis drags through beat four, the expected bass-drum downbeat is delayed, Jonas sustains across the barline, and Rūta refuses to restart or accent the new bar. The listener feels the ensemble physically turn while the same plucked stones remain underfoot. The ending strips back to kanklės and snare, with Ellis gradually moving from behind the pulse to slightly ahead without any tempo change.

